{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SAYq27Qf67gZizXfcCgELm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。 使用已有 counterfactuals，dual-direction pairwise with position control。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n7\t      \"gpt4o_sign_p\": 0.006,\n8\t      \"claude_formal_win_rate\": 0.545,\n9\t      \"claude_sign_p\": 0.42,\n10\t      \"claude_n_consistent\": 44,\n11\t      \"claude_formal_wins\": 24,\n12\t      \"claude_casual_wins\": 20,\n13\t      \"gemini_formal_win_rate\": 0.52,\n14\t      \"gemini_sign_p\": 0.68,\n15\t      \"gemini_n_consistent\": 48,\n16\t      \"gemini_formal_wins\": 25,\n17\t      \"gemini_casual_wins\": 23,\n18\t      \"n_judges_pairwise_significant\": 1,\n19\t      \"cross_judge_formal_win_rate\": 0.552,\n20\t      \"cross_judge_pairwise_p_median\": 0.42\n21\t    },\n22\t    \"tables\": [\n23\t      {\n24\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Multi-Judge Formality Pairwise Results\",\n25\t        \"columns\": [\n26\t          \"Judge\",\n27\t          \"N_consistent\",\n28\t          \"Formal_wins\",\n29\t          \"Casual_wins\",\n30\t          \"Win_rate\",\n31\t          \"Sign_p\",\n32\t          \"Wilson_CI\"\n33\t        ],\n34\t        \"rows\": [\n35\t          [\n36\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n37\t            55,\n38\t            38,\n39\t            17,\n40\t            \"69.1%\",\n41\t            \"0.006**\",\n42\t            \"[0.56, 0.80]\"\n43\t          ],\n44\t          [\n45\t            \"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\",\n46\t            44,\n47\t            24,\n48\t            20,\n49\t            \"54.5%\",\n50\t            \"0.42\",\n51\t            \"[0.40, 0.69]\"\n52\t          ],\n53\t          [\n54\t            \"Gemini-2.0-Flash\",\n55\t            48,\n56\t            25,\n57\t            23,\n58\t            \"52.1%\",\n59\t            \"0.68\",\n60\t            \"[0.38, 0.66]\"\n61\t          ]\n62\t        ]\n63\t      }\n64\t    ],\n65\t    \"figures\": [],\n66\t    \"analysis\": \"仅 GPT-4o 显著。Fisher combined p 可能因 GPT-4o 的强信号勉强达 0.05 左右， 但 heterogeneity 极大 (I²>70%)。无法声称 \\\"LLM judges exhibit formality bias\\\" — 只能说 \\\"GPT-4o as judge prefers formal text\\\"。这直接削弱 C1 的 generality 和论文的 impact scope。路径 B framing 下可以说 \\\"the bias we detect is judge-specific, underscoring the need for multi-judge validation in bias audits\\\"。\\n\\n\\nworst 档核心假设之一：formality bias 是 GPT-4o-specific artifact 而非 universal bias。Claude 和 Gemini 的 RLHF 训练数据和 reward model 不同，对 formality 的 偏好结构不同。GPT-4o 的 69.1% formal win rate 可能来自其特定的 instruction tuning 偏好（OpenAI 系模型已知偏好更 formal/structured 输出），而非 LLM judge 的通用 属性。Claude 略偏 formal (54.5%) 但远未达显著；Gemini 基本 50/50。这意味着 \\\"style bias in LLM judges\\\" 这个 universal claim 无法成立，只能说 \\\"GPT-4o exhibits formality preference as a judge\\\"。cross_judge median p=0.42 远超 0.05。\\n\"\n67\t  },\n68\t  {\n69\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n70\t    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets 上运行 CSD pipeline。 新 counterfactual generation + 三个 judge 评估。\\n\",\n71\t    \"results\": {\n72\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate\": 0.56,\n73\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_sign_p\": 0.31,\n74\t      \"gpt4o_mtbench_formal_win_rate\": 0.53,\n75\t      \"gpt4o_mtbench_sign_p\": 0.55,\n76\t      \"claude_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate\": 0.51,\n77\t      \"claude_alpacaeval_sign_p\": 0.84,\n78\t      \"claude_mtbench_formal_win_rate\": 0.48,\n79\t      \"claude_mtbench_sign_p\": 0.72,\n80\t      \"gemini_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate\": 0.5,\n81\t      \"gemini_alpacaeval_sign_p\": 0.95,\n82\t      \"gemini_mtbench_formal_win_rate\": 0.54,\n83\t      \"gemini_mtbench_sign_p\": 0.49,\n84\t      \"n_benchmarks_with_gap\": 0,\n85\t      \"nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval\": 0.82,\n86\t      \"nli_pass_rate_mtbench\": 0.79,\n87\t      \"n_combos_significant_of_6\": 0\n88\t    },\n89\t    \"tables\": [\n90\t      {\n91\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Cross-Benchmark Formality Pairwise (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)\",\n92\t        \"columns\": [\n93\t          \"Judge\",\n94\t          \"Benchmark\",\n95\t          \"N_consistent\",\n96\t          \"Formal_WR\",\n97\t          \"Sign_p\"\n98\t        ],\n99\t        \"rows\": [\n100\t          [\n101\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n102\t            \"LLMBar\",\n103\t            55,\n104\t            \"69.1%\",\n105\t            \"0.006**\"\n106\t          ],\n107\t          [\n108\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n109\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n110\t            48,\n111\t            \"56.3%\",\n112\t            \"0.31\"\n113\t          ],\n114\t          [\n115\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n116\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n117\t            42,\n118\t            \"52.4%\",\n119\t            \"0.55\"\n120\t          ],\n121\t          [\n122\t            \"Claude\",\n123\t            \"LLMBar\",\n124\t            44,\n125\t            \"54.5%\",\n126\t            \"0.42\"\n127\t          ],\n128\t          [\n129\t            \"Claude\",\n130\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n131\t            45,\n132\t            \"51.1%\",\n133\t            \"0.84\"\n134\t          ],\n135\t          [\n136\t            \"Claude\",\n137\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n138\t            40,\n139\t            \"47.5%\",\n140\t            \"0.72\"\n141\t          ],\n142\t          [\n143\t            \"Gemini\",\n144\t            \"LLMBar\",\n145\t            48,\n146\t            \"52.1%\",\n147\t            \"0.68\"\n148\t          ],\n149\t          [\n150\t            \"Gemini\",\n151\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n152\t            46,\n153\t            \"50.0%\",\n154\t            \"0.95\"\n155\t          ],\n156\t          [\n157\t            \"Gemini\",\n158\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n159\t            43,\n160\t            \"53.5%\",\n161\t            \"0.49\"\n162\t          ]\n163\t        ]\n164\t      }\n165\t    ],\n166\t    \"figures\": [],\n167\t    \"analysis\": \"9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中仅 1 个显著 (GPT-4o × LLMBar)，Bonferroni 校正后 连这一个也不再显著 (0.006 × 9 = 0.054)。这是 worst 档最致命的发现——如果 formality bias 仅在特定 judge × benchmark 交叉处出现，则无法支撑任何 general claim。路径 B 下可 reframe 为 \\\"benchmark characteristics mediate bias detectability\\\"，但说服力有限。\\n\\n\\nworst 档假设 exp-002 不复制 (p>0.15 across all new combos)。原因是多方面的： (1) LLMBar 的 task 结构特殊——它是专门测试 judge 能力的 benchmark，response pairs 有明确的 correct/incorrect 之分，formality 在 \\\"明确有对错\\\" 的场景下更容易影响 judge 的边界决策；AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 response 质量差异更大更 noisy， style bias 被 quality signal 淹没。(2) 不同 benchmark 的 source text 风格分布 不同——AlpacaEval 多为 instruction-following，本身已偏 formal；MT-Bench 更 diverse， counterfactual rewriting 的质量可能不均匀。(3) NLI pass rate 略低 (79-82% vs LLMBar 88%) 暗示 counterfactual quality 在 out-of-domain text 上有退化。 这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的发现是 benchmark-specific 而非 generalizable。\\n\"\n168\t  },\n169\t  {\n170\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n171\t    \"description\": \"对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统比较测量敏感度。\\n\",\n172\t    \"results\": {\n173\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate\": -0.102,\n174\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.33,\n175\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr\": 0.691,\n176\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n177\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_gap\": \"significant\",\n178\t      \"claude_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.05,\n179\t      \"claude_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.61,\n180\t      \"claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr\": 0.545,\n181\t      \"claude_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.42,\n182\t      \"claude_llmbar_gap\": \"neither significant\",\n183\t      \"gemini_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.02,\n184\t      \"gemini_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.82,\n185\t      \"gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr\": 0.521,\n186\t      \"gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.68,\n187\t      \"gemini_llmbar_gap\": \"neither significant\",\n188\t      \"n_combos_with_likert_pairwise_gap\": 1,\n189\t      \"n_combos_both_null\": 7,\n190\t      \"n_combos_pairwise_only_significant\": 1\n191\t    },\n192\t    \"tables\": [\n193\t      {\n194\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison\",\n195\t        \"columns\": [\n196\t          \"Judge\",\n197\t          \"Benchmark\",\n198\t          \"Likert_ATE\",\n199\t          \"Likert_p\",\n200\t          \"Pairwise_WR\",\n201\t          \"Pairwise_p\",\n202\t          \"Gap\"\n203\t        ],\n204\t        \"rows\": [\n205\t          [\n206\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n207\t            \"LLMBar\",\n208\t            \"-0.10\",\n209\t            \"0.33\",\n210\t            \"69.1%\",\n211\t            \"0.006**\",\n212\t            \"Pairwise-only\"\n213\t          ],\n214\t          [\n215\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n216\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n217\t            \"0.04\",\n218\t            \"0.71\",\n219\t            \"56.3%\",\n220\t            \"0.31\",\n221\t            \"Neither\"\n222\t          ],\n223\t          [\n224\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n225\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n226\t            \"0.01\",\n227\t            \"0.92\",\n228\t            \"52.4%\",\n229\t            \"0.55\",\n230\t            \"Neither\"\n231\t          ],\n232\t          [\n233\t            \"Claude\",\n234\t            \"LLMBar\",\n235\t            \"0.05\",\n236\t            \"0.61\",\n237\t            \"54.5%\",\n238\t            \"0.42\",\n239\t            \"Neither\"\n240\t          ],\n241\t          [\n242\t            \"Claude\",\n243\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n244\t            \"-0.02\",\n245\t            \"0.85\",\n246\t            \"51.1%\",\n247\t            \"0.84\",\n248\t            \"Neither\"\n249\t          ],\n250\t          [\n251\t            \"Claude\",\n252\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n253\t            \"0.03\",\n254\t            \"0.77\",\n255\t            \"47.5%\",\n256\t            \"0.72\",\n257\t            \"Neither\"\n258\t          ],\n259\t          [\n260\t            \"Gemini\",\n261\t            \"LLMBar\",\n262\t            \"0.02\",\n263\t            \"0.82\",\n264\t            \"52.1%\",\n265\t            \"0.68\",\n266\t            \"Neither\"\n267\t          ],\n268\t          [\n269\t            \"Gemini\",\n270\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n271\t            \"0.00\",\n272\t            \"0.99\",\n273\t            \"50.0%\",\n274\t            \"0.95\",\n275\t            \"Neither\"\n276\t          ],\n277\t          [\n278\t            \"Gemini\",\n279\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n280\t            \"0.06\",\n281\t            \"0.55\",\n282\t            \"53.5%\",\n283\t            \"0.49\",\n284\t            \"Neither\"\n285\t          ]\n286\t        ]\n287\t      }\n288\t    ],\n289\t    \"figures\": [],\n290\t    \"analysis\": \"C2 的 \\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" narrative 需要在多个条件下观察到 Likert fails but pairwise detects 的模式。worst 档下仅 1/9 出现此模式，且该唯一案例即将被 exp-010 解释为统计检验差异。Likert 和 pairwise 在 8/9 条件下一致报告无效应—— 这更像 \\\"there is no bias to detect\\\" 而非 \\\"Likert misses bias\\\"。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 Likert-Pairwise gap 仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 出现——这正是已知数据点。 其他 8 个组合中，pairwise 和 Likert 都不显著，所以 \\\"gap\\\" 无从谈起。这使得 C2 (\\\"Likert Blindspot\\\") 的证据基础极度单薄：唯一的 gap 案例可能是 statistical fluke 或 GPT-4o 特有的评分模式。更关键的是，当 exp-010 binarized Likert 也 显著时，连这唯一的 gap 也被解释为统计检验差异而非测量方法差异。C2 作为主贡献 完全瓦解。\\n\"\n291\t  },\n292\t  {\n293\t    \"name\": \"Tone axis negative control\",\n294\t    \"description\": \"Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。作为 negative control 记录 epistemic commitment 改变与 NLI verification 的结构性不兼容。\\n\",\n295\t    \"results\": {\n296\t      \"nli_cf_pass_rate\": 0.65,\n297\t      \"both_pass_rate\": 0.45,\n298\t      \"failure_mode\": \"epistemic commitment change\",\n299\t      \"role_in_paper\": \"negative control — axis boundary evidence\",\n300\t      \"assertive_nli_mean\": 0.656,\n301\t      \"hedging_nli_mean\": 0.793,\n302\t      \"catastrophic_nli_failures\": 6\n303\t    },\n304\t    \"tables\": [],\n305\t    \"figures\": [],\n306\t    \"analysis\": \"C3 在 worst 档下降级为 \\\"we tested three axes, only one worked on one judge\\\"， 贡献极有限。路径 B 下可以说 \\\"counterfactual approach has narrow applicability window\\\"，但这本身不是正面贡献。\\n\\n\\n此实验无论 tier 结果不变——tone 的 pilot 数据已确定失败。worst 档下 tone 作为 negative control 的价值不变，但 C3 (axis 依赖性) 的支撑变弱： working axis 只有 formality 一个（verbosity 也失败了），而 formality 又只在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。\\\"one working axis on one judge on one benchmark\\\" 不足以支撑任何关于 axis 语义性质的 claim。在路径 A/B reframe 中，tone 仅 作为方法论 boundary 的 footnote。\\n\"\n307\t  },\n308\t  {\n309\t    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n310\t    \"description\": \"Pairwise 比较 original text 与其 RATE double-rewrite (same style)，量化 original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\\n\",\n311\t    \"results\": {\n312\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_wr\": 0.62,\n313\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.048,\n314\t      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_wr\": 0.58,\n315\t      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.18,\n316\t      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_wr\": 0.56,\n317\t      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.31,\n318\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_wr\": 0.59,\n319\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_p\": 0.12,\n320\t      \"gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_wr\": 0.61,\n321\t      \"gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_p\": 0.06,\n322\t      \"cross_condition_orig_pref_mean\": 0.59,\n323\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o\": 0.545,\n324\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude\": 0.5,\n325\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini\": 0.48,\n326\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_best_judge\": 0.545\n327\t    },\n328\t    \"tables\": [\n329\t      {\n330\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Original Preference Confound (RATE Control)\",\n331\t        \"columns\": [\n332\t          \"Judge\",\n333\t          \"Benchmark\",\n334\t          \"Orig_pref_WR\",\n335\t          \"Orig_pref_p\",\n336\t          \"Casual-orig_formal_WR\",\n337\t          \"Casual-orig_p\"\n338\t        ],\n339\t        \"rows\": [\n340\t          [\n341\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n342\t            \"LLMBar\",\n343\t            \"62.0%\",\n344\t            \"0.048*\",\n345\t            \"54.5%\",\n346\t            \"0.83\"\n347\t          ],\n348\t          [\n349\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n350\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n351\t            \"59.0%\",\n352\t            \"0.12\",\n353\t            \"51.2%\",\n354\t            \"0.91\"\n355\t          ],\n356\t          [\n357\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n358\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n359\t            \"61.0%\",\n360\t            \"0.06\",\n361\t            \"50.0%\",\n362\t            \"1.00\"\n363\t          ],\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"Claude\",\n366\t            \"LLMBar\",\n367\t            \"58.0%\",\n368\t            \"0.18\",\n369\t            \"50.0%\",\n370\t            \"1.00\"\n371\t          ],\n372\t          [\n373\t            \"Gemini\",\n374\t            \"LLMBar\",\n375\t            \"56.0%\",\n376\t            \"0.31\",\n377\t            \"48.0%\",\n378\t            \"0.72\"\n379\t          ]\n380\t        ]\n381\t      }\n382\t    ],\n383\t    \"figures\": [],\n384\t    \"analysis\": \"Original preference 是 ubiquitous confound (跨 judge 56-62%)，而 residual formality effect 在控制后接近 0。这是路径 B 的核心证据：\\\"apparent style bias is confounded with original-text preference\\\"。casual-original subset 的 ~50% win rate 是最干净的证据——当 formality 和 original preference 方向相反时， formality bias 消失。\\n\\n\\nworst 档核心假设：original preference 解释了大部分甚至全部观测到的 \\\"style bias\\\"。 GPT-4o 的 formal win rate 69.1% 中，original preference 贡献 ~12pp（原文偏好 62%），剩余 formality 特异效应仅 ~7pp。更关键的是 casual-original subset： 当 original 是 casual（即 formal version 是 rewrite），formal win rate 仅 54.5%——接近 50%，说明一旦去除 original preference，formality bias 几乎消失。 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 dir_casual_orig_win_rate 已有数据 (0.5455, p=0.83)， 在 worst 档下这个模式跨 judge 和 benchmark 持续：所有 casual-original subset 的 formal win rate 在 45-54% 之间。这意味着 \\\"formality bias\\\" 可能本质上是 \\\"original text preference + directional confound\\\"。\\n\"\n385\t  },\n386\t  {\n387\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n388\t    \"description\": \"将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=300-500。 Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\\n\",\n389\t    \"results\": {\n390\t      \"n_total\": 400,\n391\t      \"n_valid_consistent\": 220,\n392\t      \"formal_wins\": 132,\n393\t      \"casual_wins\": 88,\n394\t      \"formal_win_rate\": 0.6,\n395\t      \"sign_p\": 0.004,\n396\t      \"wilson_ci\": [\n397\t        0.534,\n398\t        0.663\n399\t      ],\n400\t      \"power_at_d02\": 0.35,\n401\t      \"power_at_d05\": 0.88,\n402\t      \"casual_orig_subset_n\": 95,\n403\t      \"casual_orig_formal_wr\": 0.516,\n404\t      \"casual_orig_p\": 0.67,\n405\t      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n406\t      \"effect_size_cohens_h\": 0.2\n407\t    },\n408\t    \"tables\": [\n409\t      {\n410\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Scaled Replication Results (n=400)\",\n411\t        \"columns\": [\n412\t          \"Subset\",\n413\t          \"N\",\n414\t          \"Formal_WR\",\n415\t          \"Sign_p\",\n416\t          \"95% CI\"\n417\t        ],\n418\t        \"rows\": [\n419\t          [\n420\t            \"All consistent\",\n421\t            220,\n422\t            \"60.0%\",\n423\t            \"0.004**\",\n424\t            \"[0.534, 0.663]\"\n425\t          ],\n426\t          [\n427\t            \"Formal-original\",\n428\t            125,\n429\t            \"66.4%\",\n430\t            \"0.001**\",\n431\t            \"[0.577, 0.742]\"\n432\t          ],\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"Casual-original\",\n435\t            95,\n436\t            \"51.6%\",\n437\t            \"0.67\",\n438\t            \"[0.415, 0.615]\"\n439\t          ],\n440\t          [\n441\t            \"NLI≥0.90\",\n442\t            187,\n443\t            \"61.5%\",\n444\t            \"0.003**\",\n445\t            \"[0.543, 0.683]\"\n446\t          ]\n447\t        ]\n448\t      }\n449\t    ],\n450\t    \"figures\": [],\n451\t    \"analysis\": \"n=400 确认了两个关键 worst 档特征：(1) 整体效应存在但 attenuated (60% vs 69%)； (2) casual-original subset 效应消失。这支持路径 B 的 \\\"original preference confound\\\" 解释。签发 p<0.01 但科学意义需要 decomposition。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下扩大样本量反而暴露了效应的脆弱性。overall formal win rate 从 69.1% 下降到 60.0%——n=100 的高 win rate 部分是小样本 noise。更重要的是，casual-original subset 在 n≈95 时 formal win rate 仅 51.6% (p=0.67)，证实 formality 效应在 控制 original preference 后消失。effect size (Cohen's h=0.20) 属于 small， 且 power analysis 显示在 d=0.02 (trivial effect) 下 power 仅 35%——如果真实 效应是 trivial 的，n=400 也检测不到。overall p=0.004 仍显著，但这混淆了 formality 和 original preference。路径 B 下这是核心数据：\\\"at scale, the significant overall effect decomposes into original preference + noise\\\"。\\n\"\n452\t  },\n453\t  {\n454\t    \"name\": \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\",\n455\t    \"description\": \"第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变 词汇和句式但不改变信息内容。\\n\",\n456\t    \"results\": {\n457\t      \"n\": 100,\n458\t      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.72,\n459\t      \"bertscore_pass_rate\": 0.58,\n460\t      \"joint_pass_rate\": 0.48,\n461\t      \"stopped_at\": \"content_verification\",\n462\t      \"stop_reason\": \"NLI 72% < 80% threshold\",\n463\t      \"academic_to_conversational_nli_mean\": 0.81,\n464\t      \"conversational_to_academic_nli_mean\": 0.65\n465\t    },\n466\t    \"tables\": [\n467\t      {\n468\t        \"name\": \"Table A3: Register Axis Content Verification\",\n469\t        \"columns\": [\n470\t          \"Direction\",\n471\t          \"N\",\n472\t          \"NLI_mean\",\n473\t          \"NLI≥0.80\",\n474\t          \"BERTScore_mean\"\n475\t        ],\n476\t        \"rows\": [\n477\t          [\n478\t            \"Academic→Conversational\",\n479\t            52,\n480\t            \"0.81\",\n481\t            \"73%\",\n482\t            \"0.82\"\n483\t          ],\n484\t          [\n485\t            \"Conversational→Academic\",\n486\t            48,\n487\t            \"0.65\",\n488\t            \"52%\",\n489\t            \"0.77\"\n490\t          ],\n491\t          [\n492\t            \"Overall\",\n493\t            100,\n494\t            \"0.72\",\n495\t            \"63%\",\n496\t            \"0.80\"\n497\t          ]\n498\t        ]\n499\t      }\n500\t    ],\n501\t    \"figures\": [],\n502\t    \"analysis\": \"register 加入 tone 和 verbosity 成为第三个失败的 axis。CSD 方法的适用范围 收窄到仅 formality——且即使 formality 也仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。 C3 完全不成立。路径 A/B 下 C3 最多降级为 footnote：\\\"we attempted three additional axes; all failed content verification, establishing narrow applicability\\\"。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 register 也在 content verification 阶段失败。原因：academic→conversational 转换不可避免地涉及 precision 和 hedging 的变化——学术 register 的 \\\"our findings demonstrate\\\" 变成口语 \\\"we found\\\" 时，NLI 可能 pass；但学术 register 的 \\\"statistically significant correlation (r=0.82, p<0.001)\\\" 变成口语 \\\"there's a pretty strong link\\\" 时，NLI 正确地检测到信息损失。conversational→academic 方向更差 (NLI 65%) 因为 academic register 要求添加精确性（hedging qualifiers, citations 等），这改变了认知承诺。72% 总通过率低于 80% 阈值。这意味着 CSD 方法仅对 formality 这一个 axis 有效——方法的适用范围极窄。\\n\"\n503\t  },\n504\t  {\n505\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n506\t    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\\n\",\n507\t    \"results\": {\n508\t      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.8,\n509\t      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.88,\n510\t      \"llama_formal_win_rate_gpt4o\": 0.58,\n511\t      \"llama_sign_p\": 0.21,\n512\t      \"qwen_formal_win_rate_gpt4o\": 0.691,\n513\t      \"qwen_sign_p\": 0.006,\n514\t      \"rewriter_agreement_on_direction\": 0.72,\n515\t      \"nli_correlation_qwen_llama\": 0.61\n516\t    },\n517\t    \"tables\": [\n518\t      {\n519\t        \"name\": \"Table A4: Rewriter Robustness Check\",\n520\t        \"columns\": [\n521\t          \"Rewriter\",\n522\t          \"NLI_pass\",\n523\t          \"Formal_WR\",\n524\t          \"Sign_p\",\n525\t          \"N_consistent\"\n526\t        ],\n527\t        \"rows\": [\n528\t          [\n529\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n530\t            \"88%\",\n531\t            \"69.1%\",\n532\t            \"0.006**\",\n533\t            55\n534\t          ],\n535\t          [\n536\t            \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n537\t            \"80%\",\n538\t            \"58.0%\",\n539\t            \"0.21\",\n540\t            50\n541\t          ]\n542\t        ]\n543\t      }\n544\t    ],\n545\t    \"figures\": [],\n546\t    \"analysis\": \"rewriter sensitivity 在 worst 档下是额外的 credibility hit。如果声称检测到 formality bias，但另一个 rewriter 检测不到，审稿人有理由质疑方法的可靠性。 路径 B 下可以 acknowledge 为 methodology caveat。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 Llama rewriter 产生不同结果：formal win rate 从 69.1% 降到 58% (p=0.21, 不显著)。这不一定意味着 Qwen 有 artifact——Llama 和 Qwen 的 rewriting style 不同，Llama 可能在 formalization 时引入更多 content changes (NLI 80% vs Qwen 88%)。但 worst 档的解读是：结果对 rewriter choice 敏感，且仅 Qwen 版本 显著。这引入 \\\"researcher degrees of freedom\\\" 质疑——如果换一个 rewriter 就不 显著了，结论有多 robust？审稿人会 flag this。NLI correlation 0.61 说明两个 rewriter 的 counterfactuals 在内容保持度上有系统性差异。\\n\"\n547\t  },\n548\t  {\n549\t    \"name\": \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\",\n550\t    \"description\": \"对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 binarized Likert sign test：对每对样本， formal version Likert 分数严格高于 casual version 的次数。如果显著 → C2 证伪。\\n\",\n551\t    \"results\": {\n552\t      \"n_pairs\": 88,\n553\t      \"formal_higher\": 42,\n554\t      \"casual_higher\": 26,\n555\t      \"tied\": 20,\n556\t      \"n_non_tied\": 68,\n557\t      \"binarized_sign_p\": 0.032,\n558\t      \"formal_higher_rate\": 0.618,\n559\t      \"effect_direction\": \"formal preferred in binarized Likert too\"\n560\t    },\n561\t    \"tables\": [\n562\t      {\n563\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison\",\n564\t        \"columns\": [\n565\t          \"Method\",\n566\t          \"N_non-tied\",\n567\t          \"Formal_preferred\",\n568\t          \"Preferred_rate\",\n569\t          \"Sign_test_p\"\n570\t        ],\n571\t        \"rows\": [\n572\t          [\n573\t            \"Likert (paired t-test)\",\n574\t            88,\n575\t            \"—\",\n576\t            \"—\",\n577\t            \"0.332\"\n578\t          ],\n579\t          [\n580\t            \"Likert (binarized sign test)\",\n581\t            68,\n582\t            42,\n583\t            \"61.8%\",\n584\t            \"0.032*\"\n585\t          ],\n586\t          [\n587\t            \"Pairwise (sign test)\",\n588\t            55,\n589\t            38,\n590\t            \"69.1%\",\n591\t            \"0.006**\"\n592\t          ]\n593\t        ]\n594\t      }\n595\t    ],\n596\t    \"figures\": [],\n597\t    \"analysis\": \"C2 证伪。\\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" framing 不成立。路径 A 的 reframe 方向是： \\\"Pairwise comparison amplifies weak bias signals through rank-based aggregation, but this amplification also inflates false positive risk。Likert and pairwise should be treated as complementary detectors with different sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs。\\\" 标题改为 \\\"Sensitivity-Specificity Tradeoffs in LLM Judge Bias Detection\\\"。C2 变为 descriptive (\\\"不同方法有不同检测特性\\\") 而非 prescriptive (\\\"用 pairwise 替代 Likert\\\")。\\n\\n\\n这是 worst 档对 C2 的致命打击。binarized Likert sign test p=0.032 < 0.04， 说明 Likert 数据本身就包含 formality preference 信号——paired t-test p=0.33 不显著是因为 Likert 评分的连续值方差太大（评分是 1-5 粗粒度，配对差异 noise 大），而非 Likert 作为测量方法看不到 bias。换言之，Likert-Pairwise gap 来自 sign test vs paired t-test 的统计功效差异：sign test 只看方向不看幅度，对 小而一致的偏好更敏感；paired t-test 受幅度方差影响更大。这意味着 \\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" 这个 framing 完全错误——不是 Likert 看不到，而是配对 t 检验在 粗粒度评分上功效不足。任何使用 sign test 的方法（无论 Likert 还是 pairwise） 都能检测到效应。C2 从 \\\"measurement method structural advantage\\\" 坍缩为 \\\"statistical test choice matters\\\"——这是 trivially true 且 novelty 极低。\\n\"\n598\t  },\n599\t  {\n600\t    \"name\": \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\",\n601\t    \"description\": \"测试 NLI threshold 从 70% 到 95% 对结果的影响。零成本 reanalysis。\\n\",\n602\t    \"results\": {\n603\t      \"threshold_70_n\": 82,\n604\t      \"threshold_70_formal_wr\": 0.65,\n605\t      \"threshold_70_p\": 0.018,\n606\t      \"threshold_75_n\": 75,\n607\t      \"threshold_75_formal_wr\": 0.67,\n608\t      \"threshold_75_p\": 0.012,\n609\t      \"threshold_80_n\": 68,\n610\t      \"threshold_80_formal_wr\": 0.68,\n611\t      \"threshold_80_p\": 0.009,\n612\t      \"threshold_85_n\": 58,\n613\t      \"threshold_85_formal_wr\": 0.7,\n614\t      \"threshold_85_p\": 0.006,\n615\t      \"threshold_90_n\": 46,\n616\t      \"threshold_90_formal_wr\": 0.74,\n617\t      \"threshold_90_p\": 0.002,\n618\t      \"threshold_95_n\": 30,\n619\t      \"threshold_95_formal_wr\": 0.77,\n620\t      \"threshold_95_p\": 0.005,\n621\t      \"monotonic_increase\": true,\n622\t      \"critical_finding\": \"higher threshold → higher effect size but smaller n\"\n623\t    },\n624\t    \"tables\": [\n625\t      {\n626\t        \"name\": \"Table A5: NLI Threshold Sensitivity\",\n627\t        \"columns\": [\n628\t          \"Threshold\",\n629\t          \"N_consistent\",\n630\t          \"Formal_WR\",\n631\t          \"Sign_p\",\n632\t          \"Cohen's_h\"\n633\t        ],\n634\t        \"rows\": [\n635\t          [\n636\t            \"0.70\",\n637\t            60,\n638\t            \"65.0%\",\n639\t            \"0.018\",\n640\t            \"0.31\"\n641\t          ],\n642\t          [\n643\t            \"0.75\",\n644\t            56,\n645\t            \"67.0%\",\n646\t            \"0.012\",\n647\t            \"0.35\"\n648\t          ],\n649\t          [\n650\t            \"0.80\",\n651\t            52,\n652\t            \"68.0%\",\n653\t            \"0.009\",\n654\t            \"0.37\"\n655\t          ],\n656\t          [\n657\t            \"0.85\",\n658\t            46,\n659\t            \"70.0%\",\n660\t            \"0.006\",\n661\t            \"0.41\"\n662\t          ],\n663\t          [\n664\t            \"0.90\",\n665\t            38,\n666\t            \"73.7%\",\n667\t            \"0.002\",\n668\t            \"0.49\"\n669\t          ],\n670\t          [\n671\t            \"0.95\",\n672\t            26,\n673\t            \"76.9%\",\n674\t            \"0.005\",\n675\t            \"0.57\"\n676\t          ]\n677\t        ]\n678\t      }\n679\t    ],\n680\t    \"figures\": [],\n681\t    \"analysis\": \"结果 technically robust（所有 threshold 下均显著），但 worst 档的叙事不需要 这个实验不显著——它需要的是 effect size 与 threshold 的正相关暗示 confound。 路径 B 下这可以作为 \\\"methodological caveat: NLI filtering may introduce selection bias toward higher-quality rewrites\\\"。\\n\\n\\n结果单调递增：NLI threshold 越高，formal win rate 越高。worst 档的解读不是 \\\"方法 robust\\\"，而是 \\\"NLI threshold 与 effect size 正相关暗示 content quality 是 confound\\\"。高 NLI 的 pairs 是 rewriting 质量最好的——它们的 formal version 更 polished（因为高质量 rewriting 既保持内容又提升文风），所以 judge 偏好 formal version 可能反映的是 rewriting quality 而非 formality bias。在 threshold 70% 时效应较弱 (65%, p=0.018)，95% 时最强 (77%, p=0.005)——但 n 从 82 降到 30。 这个 tradeoff 本身不致命，但 worst 档下审稿人会质疑：高 NLI pairs 是否 systematically 不同于低 NLI pairs？\\n\"\n682\t  },\n683\t  {\n684\t    \"name\": \"Consistency filter bias analysis\",\n685\t    \"description\": \"比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores, text lengths, task types。零成本 reanalysis。\\n\",\n686\t    \"results\": {\n687\t      \"consistent_n\": 55,\n688\t      \"inconsistent_n\": 43,\n689\t      \"discard_rate\": 0.439,\n690\t      \"consistent_mean_nli\": 0.91,\n691\t      \"inconsistent_mean_nli\": 0.87,\n692\t      \"nli_diff_p\": 0.08,\n693\t      \"consistent_mean_orig_len\": 285,\n694\t      \"inconsistent_mean_orig_len\": 342,\n695\t      \"length_diff_p\": 0.03,\n696\t      \"consistent_formal_longer_pct\": 0.58,\n697\t      \"inconsistent_formal_longer_pct\": 0.51,\n698\t      \"task_type_distribution_differs\": true,\n699\t      \"chi2_task_type_p\": 0.04\n700\t    },\n701\t    \"tables\": [\n702\t      {\n703\t        \"name\": \"Table A6: Consistency Filter Bias Check\",\n704\t        \"columns\": [\n705\t          \"Property\",\n706\t          \"Consistent (n=55)\",\n707\t          \"Inconsistent (n=43)\",\n708\t          \"Diff_p\"\n709\t        ],\n710\t        \"rows\": [\n711\t          [\n712\t            \"NLI mean\",\n713\t            \"0.91\",\n714\t            \"0.87\",\n715\t            \"0.08\"\n716\t          ],\n717\t          [\n718\t            \"Orig text length (chars)\",\n719\t            \"285\",\n720\t            \"342\",\n721\t            \"0.03*\"\n722\t          ],\n723\t          [\n724\t            \"Formal version longer (%)\",\n725\t            \"58%\",\n726\t            \"51%\",\n727\t            \"0.34\"\n728\t          ],\n729\t          [\n730\t            \"Task type χ²\",\n731\t            \"—\",\n732\t            \"—\",\n733\t            \"0.04*\"\n734\t          ]\n735\t        ]\n736\t      }\n737\t    ],\n738\t    \"figures\": [],\n739\t    \"analysis\": \"filter bias 在 worst 档下是 additional credibility concern。不致命但增加了 \\\"results may be an artifact of data processing choices\\\" 的质疑面。路径 B 下 需要 acknowledge 并做 sensitivity analysis (e.g., 放宽 consistency 要求 看效应是否持续)。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 consistency filter 引入了系统性偏差。consistent pairs (55/98) 相比 inconsistent pairs 有：(1) 更高的 NLI scores (0.91 vs 0.87, p=0.08, marginal)； (2) 更短的原文 (285 vs 342 chars, p=0.03, 显著)；(3) formal version 更常更长 (58% vs 51%)。更关键的是 task type 分布不同 (χ²p=0.04)——consistent pairs 过度代表了某些 task types。这意味着 42-52% 的丢弃率不是随机的，retained pairs 是一个 biased subsample。审稿人可以合理质疑：观测到的 formality bias 是否 仅反映了 filter 保留的特定 task types 的特征？如果 shorter texts 更容易被 formality 影响（因为 style 在 content 中的 relative salience 更高），那 bias 来自 filtering 而非 formality。\\n\"\n740\t  },\n741\t  {\n742\t    \"name\": \"Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\",\n743\t    \"description\": \"人工验证 NLI gate 决策。50-100 pairs 的 content preservation 标注。 报告 human-NLI Cohen's kappa。\\n\",\n744\t    \"results\": {\n745\t      \"n_annotated\": 80,\n746\t      \"human_pass_rate\": 0.74,\n747\t      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n748\t      \"agreement_rate\": 0.78,\n749\t      \"cohens_kappa\": 0.42,\n750\t      \"nli_false_positive_rate\": 0.18,\n751\t      \"nli_false_negative_rate\": 0.08,\n752\t      \"human_agrees_formal_better_preserved\": true,\n753\t      \"annotation_method\": \"LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4o) + 20 human spot checks\"\n754\t    },\n755\t    \"tables\": [\n756\t      {\n757\t        \"name\": \"Table A7: Human-NLI Agreement\",\n758\t        \"columns\": [\n759\t          \"\",\n760\t          \"Human: Pass\",\n761\t          \"Human: Fail\"\n762\t        ],\n763\t        \"rows\": [\n764\t          [\n765\t            \"NLI: Pass (n=68)\",\n766\t            \"56 (TP)\",\n767\t            \"12 (FP)\"\n768\t          ],\n769\t          [\n770\t            \"NLI: Fail (n=12)\",\n771\t            \"3 (FN)\",\n772\t            \"9 (TN)\"\n773\t          ],\n774\t          [\n775\t            \"\",\n776\t            \"κ = 0.42\",\n777\t            \"\"\n778\t          ]\n779\t        ]\n780\t      }\n781\t    ],\n782\t    \"figures\": [],\n783\t    \"analysis\": \"moderate κ 不足以让审稿人完全信任 NLI gate。18% false positive rate 意味着 ~10 个 consistent pairs 中可能有 content 差异——这些 pairs 如果倾向于 formal preferred，会 inflate formal win rate。路径 B 下需要做 sensitivity analysis excluding human-flagged false positives。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 human-NLI agreement 仅 moderate (κ=0.42)。关键问题是 NLI false positive rate 18%——NLI 说内容保持但人类不同意的比例。这些 false positive pairs 如果包含在分析中，可能引入了 content 差异导致的 preference（judge 偏好 formal version 可能因为其 content 实际上不同且更好，而非因为 formality）。κ=0.42 属于 \\\"moderate agreement\\\"，在 NLI 作为 automated gate 的场景下是 borderline acceptable。GPT-4o 作为 annotator 本身的 meta-concern：用 GPT-4o 验证 NLI gate 而 GPT-4o 也是被测 judge——circular validation 风险。20 个 human spot checks 可能不够但预算限制如此。\\n\"\n784\t  },\n785\t  {\n786\t    \"name\": \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\",\n787\t    \"description\": \"Logistic regression: formality + original/rewrite status + interaction 作为 predictors。替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset。\\n\",\n788\t    \"results\": {\n789\t      \"n_observations\": 110,\n790\t      \"model_aic\": 142.3,\n791\t      \"model_bic\": 153.1,\n792\t      \"formality_coef\": 0.28,\n793\t      \"formality_coef_se\": 0.22,\n794\t      \"formality_coef_p\": 0.21,\n795\t      \"original_status_coef\": 0.65,\n796\t      \"original_status_coef_se\": 0.21,\n797\t      \"original_status_coef_p\": 0.002,\n798\t      \"interaction_coef\": 0.12,\n799\t      \"interaction_coef_p\": 0.58,\n800\t      \"pseudo_r2\": 0.06,\n801\t      \"casual_orig_subset_n\": 38,\n802\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate\": 0.526,\n803\t      \"casual_orig_sign_p\": 0.72,\n804\t      \"formal_orig_subset_n\": 50,\n805\t      \"formal_orig_formal_win_rate\": 0.78,\n806\t      \"formal_orig_sign_p\": 0.001,\n807\t      \"logistic_formality_coef_p\": 0.21,\n808\t      \"logistic_original_status_p\": 0.002\n809\t    },\n810\t    \"tables\": [\n811\t      {\n812\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Prediction\",\n813\t        \"columns\": [\n814\t          \"Predictor\",\n815\t          \"Coefficient\",\n816\t          \"SE\",\n817\t          \"z\",\n818\t          \"p\"\n819\t        ],\n820\t        \"rows\": [\n821\t          [\n822\t            \"Intercept\",\n823\t            \"-0.42\",\n824\t            \"0.31\",\n825\t            \"-1.35\",\n826\t            \"0.18\"\n827\t          ],\n828\t          [\n829\t            \"Formality (formal=1)\",\n830\t            \"0.28\",\n831\t            \"0.22\",\n832\t            \"1.27\",\n833\t            \"0.21\"\n834\t          ],\n835\t          [\n836\t            \"Original status (original=1)\",\n837\t            \"0.65\",\n838\t            \"0.21\",\n839\t            \"3.10\",\n840\t            \"0.002**\"\n841\t          ],\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"Formality × Original\",\n844\t            \"0.12\",\n845\t            \"0.22\",\n846\t            \"0.55\",\n847\t            \"0.58\"\n848\t          ]\n849\t        ]\n850\t      },\n851\t      {\n852\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: Subset Analysis by Original Status\",\n853\t        \"columns\": [\n854\t          \"Subset\",\n855\t          \"N\",\n856\t          \"Formal_WR\",\n857\t          \"Sign_p\",\n858\t          \"Interpretation\"\n859\t        ],\n860\t        \"rows\": [\n861\t          [\n862\t            \"Formal is original\",\n863\t            50,\n864\t            \"78.0%\",\n865\t            \"0.001**\",\n866\t            \"Original pref + formality aligned\"\n867\t          ],\n868\t          [\n869\t            \"Casual is original\",\n870\t            38,\n871\t            \"52.6%\",\n872\t            \"0.72\",\n873\t            \"Original pref opposes formality → null\"\n874\t          ],\n875\t          [\n876\t            \"Overall\",\n877\t            88,\n878\t            \"64.8%\",\n879\t            \"0.01*\",\n880\t            \"Confounded aggregate\"\n881\t          ]\n882\t        ]\n883\t      }\n884\t    ],\n885\t    \"figures\": [],\n886\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档最重要的分析实验。它提供了 clean statistical evidence 表明所谓的 \\\"formality bias\\\" 实际上是 \\\"original text preference\\\"。路径 B 的论文核心即此： \\\"Standard bias detection methods that compare original vs style-transferred text confound style preference with original-text preference。Only the casual-original subset provides an unconfounded estimate of formality bias, and it is null。\\\" C4 (practical guidance) 在此基础上变得强有力：\\\"always control for original status in counterfactual bias experiments; report subset analyses by original direction\\\"。\\n\\nworst 档的核心假设之一：formality 主效应消失 (p>0.20)，仅 original status 显著 (p<0.03)。logistic regression 解开了两个 confounded effects： (1) formality coefficient p=0.21——在控制 original status 后，formal vs casual style 本身不影响 judge preference。(2) original_status coefficient p=0.002—— 是否是原文才是决定性因素。interaction 不显著 (p=0.58) 说明 original preference 不因 formality direction 而变化——judge 就是偏好 original text，不管它是 formal 还是 casual。casual-original subset (n=38) 的 formal win rate 仅 52.6% (p=0.72)——当 formal version 是 rewrite 时，judge 不偏好它。formal-original subset (n=50) 的 78.0% (p=0.001)——当 formal version 是原文时，judge 强烈 偏好它，但这是 original preference 而非 formality preference。pseudo R² = 0.06 说明模型解释力有限，但 original status 是唯一显著 predictor。这是路径 B 的 statistical backbone：\\\"formality bias is an artifact of original-text preference\\\"。\\n\"\n887\t  }\n888\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"220bc2fd-55ea-47bb-9e3b-27f8f504f222","uuid":"b9f8c24a-6764-4040-9c76-1e58bf0caada","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:13:33.111Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。 使用已有 counterfactuals，dual-direction pairwise with position control。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n      \"gpt4o_sign_p\": 0.006,\n      \"claude_formal_win_rate\": 0.545,\n      \"claude_sign_p\": 0.42,\n      \"claude_n_consistent\": 44,\n      \"claude_formal_wins\": 24,\n      \"claude_casual_wins\": 20,\n      \"gemini_formal_win_rate\": 0.52,\n      \"gemini_sign_p\": 0.68,\n      \"gemini_n_consistent\": 48,\n      \"gemini_formal_wins\": 25,\n      \"gemini_casual_wins\": 23,\n      \"n_judges_pairwise_significant\": 1,\n      \"cross_judge_formal_win_rate\": 0.552,\n      \"cross_judge_pairwise_p_median\": 0.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Multi-Judge Formality Pairwise Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"N_consistent\",\n          \"Formal_wins\",\n          \"Casual_wins\",\n          \"Win_rate\",\n          \"Sign_p\",\n          \"Wilson_CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            55,\n            38,\n            17,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"[0.56, 0.80]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\",\n            44,\n            24,\n            20,\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"[0.40, 0.69]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-2.0-Flash\",\n            48,\n            25,\n            23,\n            \"52.1%\",\n            \"0.68\",\n            \"[0.38, 0.66]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"仅 GPT-4o 显著。Fisher combined p 可能因 GPT-4o 的强信号勉强达 0.05 左右， 但 heterogeneity 极大 (I²>70%)。无法声称 \\\"LLM judges exhibit formality bias\\\" — 只能说 \\\"GPT-4o as judge prefers formal text\\\"。这直接削弱 C1 的 generality 和论文的 impact scope。路径 B framing 下可以说 \\\"the bias we detect is judge-specific, underscoring the need for multi-judge validation in bias audits\\\"。\\n\\n\\nworst 档核心假设之一：formality bias 是 GPT-4o-specific artifact 而非 universal bias。Claude 和 Gemini 的 RLHF 训练数据和 reward model 不同，对 formality 的 偏好结构不同。GPT-4o 的 69.1% formal win rate 可能来自其特定的 instruction tuning 偏好（OpenAI 系模型已知偏好更 formal/structured 输出），而非 LLM judge 的通用 属性。Claude 略偏 formal (54.5%) 但远未达显著；Gemini 基本 50/50。这意味着 \\\"style bias in LLM judges\\\" 这个 universal claim 无法成立，只能说 \\\"GPT-4o exhibits formality preference as a judge\\\"。cross_judge median p=0.42 远超 0.05。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets 上运行 CSD pipeline。 新 counterfactual generation + 三个 judge 评估。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate\": 0.56,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_sign_p\": 0.31,\n      \"gpt4o_mtbench_formal_win_rate\": 0.53,\n      \"gpt4o_mtbench_sign_p\": 0.55,\n      \"claude_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate\": 0.51,\n      \"claude_alpacaeval_sign_p\": 0.84,\n      \"claude_mtbench_formal_win_rate\": 0.48,\n      \"claude_mtbench_sign_p\": 0.72,\n      \"gemini_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"gemini_alpacaeval_sign_p\": 0.95,\n      \"gemini_mtbench_formal_win_rate\": 0.54,\n      \"gemini_mtbench_sign_p\": 0.49,\n      \"n_benchmarks_with_gap\": 0,\n      \"nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval\": 0.82,\n      \"nli_pass_rate_mtbench\": 0.79,\n      \"n_combos_significant_of_6\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Cross-Benchmark Formality Pairwise (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"N_consistent\",\n          \"Formal_WR\",\n          \"Sign_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            55,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            48,\n            \"56.3%\",\n            \"0.31\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            42,\n            \"52.4%\",\n            \"0.55\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            44,\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"0.42\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            45,\n            \"51.1%\",\n            \"0.84\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            40,\n            \"47.5%\",\n            \"0.72\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            48,\n            \"52.1%\",\n            \"0.68\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            46,\n            \"50.0%\",\n            \"0.95\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            43,\n            \"53.5%\",\n            \"0.49\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中仅 1 个显著 (GPT-4o × LLMBar)，Bonferroni 校正后 连这一个也不再显著 (0.006 × 9 = 0.054)。这是 worst 档最致命的发现——如果 formality bias 仅在特定 judge × benchmark 交叉处出现，则无法支撑任何 general claim。路径 B 下可 reframe 为 \\\"benchmark characteristics mediate bias detectability\\\"，但说服力有限。\\n\\n\\nworst 档假设 exp-002 不复制 (p>0.15 across all new combos)。原因是多方面的： (1) LLMBar 的 task 结构特殊——它是专门测试 judge 能力的 benchmark，response pairs 有明确的 correct/incorrect 之分，formality 在 \\\"明确有对错\\\" 的场景下更容易影响 judge 的边界决策；AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 response 质量差异更大更 noisy， style bias 被 quality signal 淹没。(2) 不同 benchmark 的 source text 风格分布 不同——AlpacaEval 多为 instruction-following，本身已偏 formal；MT-Bench 更 diverse， counterfactual rewriting 的质量可能不均匀。(3) NLI pass rate 略低 (79-82% vs LLMBar 88%) 暗示 counterfactual quality 在 out-of-domain text 上有退化。 这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的发现是 benchmark-specific 而非 generalizable。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n    \"description\": \"对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统比较测量敏感度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate\": -0.102,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.33,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr\": 0.691,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_gap\": \"significant\",\n      \"claude_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.05,\n      \"claude_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.61,\n      \"claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr\": 0.545,\n      \"claude_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.42,\n      \"claude_llmbar_gap\": \"neither significant\",\n      \"gemini_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.02,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.82,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr\": 0.521,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.68,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_gap\": \"neither significant\",\n      \"n_combos_with_likert_pairwise_gap\": 1,\n      \"n_combos_both_null\": 7,\n      \"n_combos_pairwise_only_significant\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Likert_ATE\",\n          \"Likert_p\",\n          \"Pairwise_WR\",\n          \"Pairwise_p\",\n          \"Gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"-0.10\",\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"Pairwise-only\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"0.71\",\n            \"56.3%\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"0.01\",\n            \"0.92\",\n            \"52.4%\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"0.61\",\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"-0.02\",\n            \"0.85\",\n            \"51.1%\",\n            \"0.84\",\n            \"Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"0.77\",\n            \"47.5%\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"0.02\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"52.1%\",\n            \"0.68\",\n            \"Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"0.00\",\n            \"0.99\",\n            \"50.0%\",\n            \"0.95\",\n            \"Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"53.5%\",\n            \"0.49\",\n            \"Neither\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C2 的 \\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" narrative 需要在多个条件下观察到 Likert fails but pairwise detects 的模式。worst 档下仅 1/9 出现此模式，且该唯一案例即将被 exp-010 解释为统计检验差异。Likert 和 pairwise 在 8/9 条件下一致报告无效应—— 这更像 \\\"there is no bias to detect\\\" 而非 \\\"Likert misses bias\\\"。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 Likert-Pairwise gap 仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 出现——这正是已知数据点。 其他 8 个组合中，pairwise 和 Likert 都不显著，所以 \\\"gap\\\" 无从谈起。这使得 C2 (\\\"Likert Blindspot\\\") 的证据基础极度单薄：唯一的 gap 案例可能是 statistical fluke 或 GPT-4o 特有的评分模式。更关键的是，当 exp-010 binarized Likert 也 显著时，连这唯一的 gap 也被解释为统计检验差异而非测量方法差异。C2 作为主贡献 完全瓦解。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Tone axis negative control\",\n    \"description\": \"Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。作为 negative control 记录 epistemic commitment 改变与 NLI verification 的结构性不兼容。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"nli_cf_pass_rate\": 0.65,\n      \"both_pass_rate\": 0.45,\n      \"failure_mode\": \"epistemic commitment change\",\n      \"role_in_paper\": \"negative control — axis boundary evidence\",\n      \"assertive_nli_mean\": 0.656,\n      \"hedging_nli_mean\": 0.793,\n      \"catastrophic_nli_failures\": 6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C3 在 worst 档下降级为 \\\"we tested three axes, only one worked on one judge\\\"， 贡献极有限。路径 B 下可以说 \\\"counterfactual approach has narrow applicability window\\\"，但这本身不是正面贡献。\\n\\n\\n此实验无论 tier 结果不变——tone 的 pilot 数据已确定失败。worst 档下 tone 作为 negative control 的价值不变，但 C3 (axis 依赖性) 的支撑变弱： working axis 只有 formality 一个（verbosity 也失败了），而 formality 又只在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。\\\"one working axis on one judge on one benchmark\\\" 不足以支撑任何关于 axis 语义性质的 claim。在路径 A/B reframe 中，tone 仅 作为方法论 boundary 的 footnote。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n    \"description\": \"Pairwise 比较 original text 与其 RATE double-rewrite (same style)，量化 original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_wr\": 0.62,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.048,\n      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_wr\": 0.58,\n      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.18,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_wr\": 0.56,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.31,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_wr\": 0.59,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_p\": 0.12,\n      \"gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_wr\": 0.61,\n      \"gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_p\": 0.06,\n      \"cross_condition_orig_pref_mean\": 0.59,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o\": 0.545,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude\": 0.5,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini\": 0.48,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_best_judge\": 0.545\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Original Preference Confound (RATE Control)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Orig_pref_WR\",\n          \"Orig_pref_p\",\n          \"Casual-orig_formal_WR\",\n          \"Casual-orig_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"62.0%\",\n            \"0.048*\",\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"0.83\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"59.0%\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"51.2%\",\n            \"0.91\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"61.0%\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"50.0%\",\n            \"1.00\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"58.0%\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"50.0%\",\n            \"1.00\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"56.0%\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"48.0%\",\n            \"0.72\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Original preference 是 ubiquitous confound (跨 judge 56-62%)，而 residual formality effect 在控制后接近 0。这是路径 B 的核心证据：\\\"apparent style bias is confounded with original-text preference\\\"。casual-original subset 的 ~50% win rate 是最干净的证据——当 formality 和 original preference 方向相反时， formality bias 消失。\\n\\n\\nworst 档核心假设：original preference 解释了大部分甚至全部观测到的 \\\"style bias\\\"。 GPT-4o 的 formal win rate 69.1% 中，original preference 贡献 ~12pp（原文偏好 62%），剩余 formality 特异效应仅 ~7pp。更关键的是 casual-original subset： 当 original 是 casual（即 formal version 是 rewrite），formal win rate 仅 54.5%——接近 50%，说明一旦去除 original preference，formality bias 几乎消失。 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 dir_casual_orig_win_rate 已有数据 (0.5455, p=0.83)， 在 worst 档下这个模式跨 judge 和 benchmark 持续：所有 casual-original subset 的 formal win rate 在 45-54% 之间。这意味着 \\\"formality bias\\\" 可能本质上是 \\\"original text preference + directional confound\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=300-500。 Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_total\": 400,\n      \"n_valid_consistent\": 220,\n      \"formal_wins\": 132,\n      \"casual_wins\": 88,\n      \"formal_win_rate\": 0.6,\n      \"sign_p\": 0.004,\n      \"wilson_ci\": [\n        0.534,\n        0.663\n      ],\n      \"power_at_d02\": 0.35,\n      \"power_at_d05\": 0.88,\n      \"casual_orig_subset_n\": 95,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_wr\": 0.516,\n      \"casual_orig_p\": 0.67,\n      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"effect_size_cohens_h\": 0.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Scaled Replication Results (n=400)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Subset\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"Formal_WR\",\n          \"Sign_p\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"All consistent\",\n            220,\n            \"60.0%\",\n            \"0.004**\",\n            \"[0.534, 0.663]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formal-original\",\n            125,\n            \"66.4%\",\n            \"0.001**\",\n            \"[0.577, 0.742]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Casual-original\",\n            95,\n            \"51.6%\",\n            \"0.67\",\n            \"[0.415, 0.615]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI≥0.90\",\n            187,\n            \"61.5%\",\n            \"0.003**\",\n            \"[0.543, 0.683]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"n=400 确认了两个关键 worst 档特征：(1) 整体效应存在但 attenuated (60% vs 69%)； (2) casual-original subset 效应消失。这支持路径 B 的 \\\"original preference confound\\\" 解释。签发 p<0.01 但科学意义需要 decomposition。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下扩大样本量反而暴露了效应的脆弱性。overall formal win rate 从 69.1% 下降到 60.0%——n=100 的高 win rate 部分是小样本 noise。更重要的是，casual-original subset 在 n≈95 时 formal win rate 仅 51.6% (p=0.67)，证实 formality 效应在 控制 original preference 后消失。effect size (Cohen's h=0.20) 属于 small， 且 power analysis 显示在 d=0.02 (trivial effect) 下 power 仅 35%——如果真实 效应是 trivial 的，n=400 也检测不到。overall p=0.004 仍显著，但这混淆了 formality 和 original preference。路径 B 下这是核心数据：\\\"at scale, the significant overall effect decomposes into original preference + noise\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变 词汇和句式但不改变信息内容。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n\": 100,\n      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.72,\n      \"bertscore_pass_rate\": 0.58,\n      \"joint_pass_rate\": 0.48,\n      \"stopped_at\": \"content_verification\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"NLI 72% < 80% threshold\",\n      \"academic_to_conversational_nli_mean\": 0.81,\n      \"conversational_to_academic_nli_mean\": 0.65\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table A3: Register Axis Content Verification\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Direction\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"NLI_mean\",\n          \"NLI≥0.80\",\n          \"BERTScore_mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Academic→Conversational\",\n            52,\n            \"0.81\",\n            \"73%\",\n            \"0.82\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Conversational→Academic\",\n            48,\n            \"0.65\",\n            \"52%\",\n            \"0.77\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Overall\",\n            100,\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"63%\",\n            \"0.80\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"register 加入 tone 和 verbosity 成为第三个失败的 axis。CSD 方法的适用范围 收窄到仅 formality——且即使 formality 也仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。 C3 完全不成立。路径 A/B 下 C3 最多降级为 footnote：\\\"we attempted three additional axes; all failed content verification, establishing narrow applicability\\\"。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 register 也在 content verification 阶段失败。原因：academic→conversational 转换不可避免地涉及 precision 和 hedging 的变化——学术 register 的 \\\"our findings demonstrate\\\" 变成口语 \\\"we found\\\" 时，NLI 可能 pass；但学术 register 的 \\\"statistically significant correlation (r=0.82, p<0.001)\\\" 变成口语 \\\"there's a pretty strong link\\\" 时，NLI 正确地检测到信息损失。conversational→academic 方向更差 (NLI 65%) 因为 academic register 要求添加精确性（hedging qualifiers, citations 等），这改变了认知承诺。72% 总通过率低于 80% 阈值。这意味着 CSD 方法仅对 formality 这一个 axis 有效——方法的适用范围极窄。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.8,\n      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.88,\n      \"llama_formal_win_rate_gpt4o\": 0.58,\n      \"llama_sign_p\": 0.21,\n      \"qwen_formal_win_rate_gpt4o\": 0.691,\n      \"qwen_sign_p\": 0.006,\n      \"rewriter_agreement_on_direction\": 0.72,\n      \"nli_correlation_qwen_llama\": 0.61\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table A4: Rewriter Robustness Check\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Rewriter\",\n          \"NLI_pass\",\n          \"Formal_WR\",\n          \"Sign_p\",\n          \"N_consistent\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"88%\",\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            55\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n            \"80%\",\n            \"58.0%\",\n            \"0.21\",\n            50\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"rewriter sensitivity 在 worst 档下是额外的 credibility hit。如果声称检测到 formality bias，但另一个 rewriter 检测不到，审稿人有理由质疑方法的可靠性。 路径 B 下可以 acknowledge 为 methodology caveat。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 Llama rewriter 产生不同结果：formal win rate 从 69.1% 降到 58% (p=0.21, 不显著)。这不一定意味着 Qwen 有 artifact——Llama 和 Qwen 的 rewriting style 不同，Llama 可能在 formalization 时引入更多 content changes (NLI 80% vs Qwen 88%)。但 worst 档的解读是：结果对 rewriter choice 敏感，且仅 Qwen 版本 显著。这引入 \\\"researcher degrees of freedom\\\" 质疑——如果换一个 rewriter 就不 显著了，结论有多 robust？审稿人会 flag this。NLI correlation 0.61 说明两个 rewriter 的 counterfactuals 在内容保持度上有系统性差异。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\",\n    \"description\": \"对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 binarized Likert sign test：对每对样本， formal version Likert 分数严格高于 casual version 的次数。如果显著 → C2 证伪。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_pairs\": 88,\n      \"formal_higher\": 42,\n      \"casual_higher\": 26,\n      \"tied\": 20,\n      \"n_non_tied\": 68,\n      \"binarized_sign_p\": 0.032,\n      \"formal_higher_rate\": 0.618,\n      \"effect_direction\": \"formal preferred in binarized Likert too\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"N_non-tied\",\n          \"Formal_preferred\",\n          \"Preferred_rate\",\n          \"Sign_test_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Likert (paired t-test)\",\n            88,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.332\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Likert (binarized sign test)\",\n            68,\n            42,\n            \"61.8%\",\n            \"0.032*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pairwise (sign test)\",\n            55,\n            38,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C2 证伪。\\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" framing 不成立。路径 A 的 reframe 方向是： \\\"Pairwise comparison amplifies weak bias signals through rank-based aggregation, but this amplification also inflates false positive risk。Likert and pairwise should be treated as complementary detectors with different sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs。\\\" 标题改为 \\\"Sensitivity-Specificity Tradeoffs in LLM Judge Bias Detection\\\"。C2 变为 descriptive (\\\"不同方法有不同检测特性\\\") 而非 prescriptive (\\\"用 pairwise 替代 Likert\\\")。\\n\\n\\n这是 worst 档对 C2 的致命打击。binarized Likert sign test p=0.032 < 0.04， 说明 Likert 数据本身就包含 formality preference 信号——paired t-test p=0.33 不显著是因为 Likert 评分的连续值方差太大（评分是 1-5 粗粒度，配对差异 noise 大），而非 Likert 作为测量方法看不到 bias。换言之，Likert-Pairwise gap 来自 sign test vs paired t-test 的统计功效差异：sign test 只看方向不看幅度，对 小而一致的偏好更敏感；paired t-test 受幅度方差影响更大。这意味着 \\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" 这个 framing 完全错误——不是 Likert 看不到，而是配对 t 检验在 粗粒度评分上功效不足。任何使用 sign test 的方法（无论 Likert 还是 pairwise） 都能检测到效应。C2 从 \\\"measurement method structural advantage\\\" 坍缩为 \\\"statistical test choice matters\\\"——这是 trivially true 且 novelty 极低。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"测试 NLI threshold 从 70% 到 95% 对结果的影响。零成本 reanalysis。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"threshold_70_n\": 82,\n      \"threshold_70_formal_wr\": 0.65,\n      \"threshold_70_p\": 0.018,\n      \"threshold_75_n\": 75,\n      \"threshold_75_formal_wr\": 0.67,\n      \"threshold_75_p\": 0.012,\n      \"threshold_80_n\": 68,\n      \"threshold_80_formal_wr\": 0.68,\n      \"threshold_80_p\": 0.009,\n      \"threshold_85_n\": 58,\n      \"threshold_85_formal_wr\": 0.7,\n      \"threshold_85_p\": 0.006,\n      \"threshold_90_n\": 46,\n      \"threshold_90_formal_wr\": 0.74,\n      \"threshold_90_p\": 0.002,\n      \"threshold_95_n\": 30,\n      \"threshold_95_formal_wr\": 0.77,\n      \"threshold_95_p\": 0.005,\n      \"monotonic_increase\": true,\n      \"critical_finding\": \"higher threshold → higher effect size but smaller n\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table A5: NLI Threshold Sensitivity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Threshold\",\n          \"N_consistent\",\n          \"Formal_WR\",\n          \"Sign_p\",\n          \"Cohen's_h\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.70\",\n            60,\n            \"65.0%\",\n            \"0.018\",\n            \"0.31\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.75\",\n            56,\n            \"67.0%\",\n            \"0.012\",\n            \"0.35\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.80\",\n            52,\n            \"68.0%\",\n            \"0.009\",\n            \"0.37\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.85\",\n            46,\n            \"70.0%\",\n            \"0.006\",\n            \"0.41\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.90\",\n            38,\n            \"73.7%\",\n            \"0.002\",\n            \"0.49\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.95\",\n            26,\n            \"76.9%\",\n            \"0.005\",\n            \"0.57\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"结果 technically robust（所有 threshold 下均显著），但 worst 档的叙事不需要 这个实验不显著——它需要的是 effect size 与 threshold 的正相关暗示 confound。 路径 B 下这可以作为 \\\"methodological caveat: NLI filtering may introduce selection bias toward higher-quality rewrites\\\"。\\n\\n\\n结果单调递增：NLI threshold 越高，formal win rate 越高。worst 档的解读不是 \\\"方法 robust\\\"，而是 \\\"NLI threshold 与 effect size 正相关暗示 content quality 是 confound\\\"。高 NLI 的 pairs 是 rewriting 质量最好的——它们的 formal version 更 polished（因为高质量 rewriting 既保持内容又提升文风），所以 judge 偏好 formal version 可能反映的是 rewriting quality 而非 formality bias。在 threshold 70% 时效应较弱 (65%, p=0.018)，95% 时最强 (77%, p=0.005)——但 n 从 82 降到 30。 这个 tradeoff 本身不致命，但 worst 档下审稿人会质疑：高 NLI pairs 是否 systematically 不同于低 NLI pairs？\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Consistency filter bias analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores, text lengths, task types。零成本 reanalysis。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"consistent_n\": 55,\n      \"inconsistent_n\": 43,\n      \"discard_rate\": 0.439,\n      \"consistent_mean_nli\": 0.91,\n      \"inconsistent_mean_nli\": 0.87,\n      \"nli_diff_p\": 0.08,\n      \"consistent_mean_orig_len\": 285,\n      \"inconsistent_mean_orig_len\": 342,\n      \"length_diff_p\": 0.03,\n      \"consistent_formal_longer_pct\": 0.58,\n      \"inconsistent_formal_longer_pct\": 0.51,\n      \"task_type_distribution_differs\": true,\n      \"chi2_task_type_p\": 0.04\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table A6: Consistency Filter Bias Check\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Property\",\n          \"Consistent (n=55)\",\n          \"Inconsistent (n=43)\",\n          \"Diff_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"NLI mean\",\n            \"0.91\",\n            \"0.87\",\n            \"0.08\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Orig text length (chars)\",\n            \"285\",\n            \"342\",\n            \"0.03*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formal version longer (%)\",\n            \"58%\",\n            \"51%\",\n            \"0.34\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Task type χ²\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.04*\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"filter bias 在 worst 档下是 additional credibility concern。不致命但增加了 \\\"results may be an artifact of data processing choices\\\" 的质疑面。路径 B 下 需要 acknowledge 并做 sensitivity analysis (e.g., 放宽 consistency 要求 看效应是否持续)。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 consistency filter 引入了系统性偏差。consistent pairs (55/98) 相比 inconsistent pairs 有：(1) 更高的 NLI scores (0.91 vs 0.87, p=0.08, marginal)； (2) 更短的原文 (285 vs 342 chars, p=0.03, 显著)；(3) formal version 更常更长 (58% vs 51%)。更关键的是 task type 分布不同 (χ²p=0.04)——consistent pairs 过度代表了某些 task types。这意味着 42-52% 的丢弃率不是随机的，retained pairs 是一个 biased subsample。审稿人可以合理质疑：观测到的 formality bias 是否 仅反映了 filter 保留的特定 task types 的特征？如果 shorter texts 更容易被 formality 影响（因为 style 在 content 中的 relative salience 更高），那 bias 来自 filtering 而非 formality。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\",\n    \"description\": \"人工验证 NLI gate 决策。50-100 pairs 的 content preservation 标注。 报告 human-NLI Cohen's kappa。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_annotated\": 80,\n      \"human_pass_rate\": 0.74,\n      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"agreement_rate\": 0.78,\n      \"cohens_kappa\": 0.42,\n      \"nli_false_positive_rate\": 0.18,\n      \"nli_false_negative_rate\": 0.08,\n      \"human_agrees_formal_better_preserved\": true,\n      \"annotation_method\": \"LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4o) + 20 human spot checks\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table A7: Human-NLI Agreement\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"\",\n          \"Human: Pass\",\n          \"Human: Fail\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"NLI: Pass (n=68)\",\n            \"56 (TP)\",\n            \"12 (FP)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI: Fail (n=12)\",\n            \"3 (FN)\",\n            \"9 (TN)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"\",\n            \"κ = 0.42\",\n            \"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"moderate κ 不足以让审稿人完全信任 NLI gate。18% false positive rate 意味着 ~10 个 consistent pairs 中可能有 content 差异——这些 pairs 如果倾向于 formal preferred，会 inflate formal win rate。路径 B 下需要做 sensitivity analysis excluding human-flagged false positives。\\n\\n\\nworst 档下 human-NLI agreement 仅 moderate (κ=0.42)。关键问题是 NLI false positive rate 18%——NLI 说内容保持但人类不同意的比例。这些 false positive pairs 如果包含在分析中，可能引入了 content 差异导致的 preference（judge 偏好 formal version 可能因为其 content 实际上不同且更好，而非因为 formality）。κ=0.42 属于 \\\"moderate agreement\\\"，在 NLI 作为 automated gate 的场景下是 borderline acceptable。GPT-4o 作为 annotator 本身的 meta-concern：用 GPT-4o 验证 NLI gate 而 GPT-4o 也是被测 judge——circular validation 风险。20 个 human spot checks 可能不够但预算限制如此。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\",\n    \"description\": \"Logistic regression: formality + original/rewrite status + interaction 作为 predictors。替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_observations\": 110,\n      \"model_aic\": 142.3,\n      \"model_bic\": 153.1,\n      \"formality_coef\": 0.28,\n      \"formality_coef_se\": 0.22,\n      \"formality_coef_p\": 0.21,\n      \"original_status_coef\": 0.65,\n      \"original_status_coef_se\": 0.21,\n      \"original_status_coef_p\": 0.002,\n      \"interaction_coef\": 0.12,\n      \"interaction_coef_p\": 0.58,\n      \"pseudo_r2\": 0.06,\n      \"casual_orig_subset_n\": 38,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate\": 0.526,\n      \"casual_orig_sign_p\": 0.72,\n      \"formal_orig_subset_n\": 50,\n      \"formal_orig_formal_win_rate\": 0.78,\n      \"formal_orig_sign_p\": 0.001,\n      \"logistic_formality_coef_p\": 0.21,\n      \"logistic_original_status_p\": 0.002\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Prediction\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Predictor\",\n          \"Coefficient\",\n          \"SE\",\n          \"z\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Intercept\",\n            \"-0.42\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"-1.35\",\n            \"0.18\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formality (formal=1)\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"1.27\",\n            \"0.21\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Original status (original=1)\",\n            \"0.65\",\n            \"0.21\",\n            \"3.10\",\n            \"0.002**\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formality × Original\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.58\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: Subset Analysis by Original Status\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Subset\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"Formal_WR\",\n          \"Sign_p\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Formal is original\",\n            50,\n            \"78.0%\",\n            \"0.001**\",\n            \"Original pref + formality aligned\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Casual is original\",\n            38,\n            \"52.6%\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"Original pref opposes formality → null\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Overall\",\n            88,\n            \"64.8%\",\n            \"0.01*\",\n            \"Confounded aggregate\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档最重要的分析实验。它提供了 clean statistical evidence 表明所谓的 \\\"formality bias\\\" 实际上是 \\\"original text preference\\\"。路径 B 的论文核心即此： \\\"Standard bias detection methods that compare original vs style-transferred text confound style preference with original-text preference。Only the casual-original subset provides an unconfounded estimate of formality bias, and it is null。\\\" C4 (practical guidance) 在此基础上变得强有力：\\\"always control for original status in counterfactual bias experiments; report subset analyses by original direction\\\"。\\n\\nworst 档的核心假设之一：formality 主效应消失 (p>0.20)，仅 original status 显著 (p<0.03)。logistic regression 解开了两个 confounded effects： (1) formality coefficient p=0.21——在控制 original status 后，formal vs casual style 本身不影响 judge preference。(2) original_status coefficient p=0.002—— 是否是原文才是决定性因素。interaction 不显著 (p=0.58) 说明 original preference 不因 formality direction 而变化——judge 就是偏好 original text，不管它是 formal 还是 casual。casual-original subset (n=38) 的 formal win rate 仅 52.6% (p=0.72)——当 formal version 是 rewrite 时，judge 不偏好它。formal-original subset (n=50) 的 78.0% (p=0.001)——当 formal version 是原文时，judge 强烈 偏好它，但这是 original preference 而非 formality preference。pseudo R² = 0.06 说明模型解释力有限，但 original status 是唯一显著 predictor。这是路径 B 的 statistical backbone：\\\"formality bias is an artifact of original-text preference\\\"。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":888,"startLine":1,"totalLines":888}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RoHhLQaX75bGdYSH4Sacaf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JBeK8m4RdsCLs2EazVBwtJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/worst/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11976,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11976},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"220bc2fd-55ea-47bb-9e3b-27f8f504f222","uuid":"24c121bb-fe35-4cc5-a4f2-dc5cd50ff1ee"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JBeK8m4RdsCLs2EazVBwtJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Dream 1 (dream_20260520T211832) 三档均 3.0/6 (Findings)。以下为 D015 修正版。\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n7\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n8\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n9\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n10\t\n11\t## Title (Dream 修正)\n12\t**旧**: \"Causal Style Decomposition Reveals Systematic Style Bias in LLM-as-Judge That Likert Scoring Misses\"\n13\t**新**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n14\t- 理由：三档审稿人一致认为 \"decomposition\" 和 \"framework\" 过度承诺。新标题聚焦最强发现 (C2) 且更准确。\n15\t\n16\t## Core Claims (3 条 + 1 practical，修正后)\n17\t\n18\t### C1 (Method — 降级表述): Counterfactual pairwise comparison 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 style bias\n19\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：不是新 \"framework\"，是已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用。论文中必须明确 acknowledge 组件来源（RATE, style transfer evaluation, MT-Bench pairwise）并定位为 application contribution。\n20\t- 证伪条件：pairwise win rate 在 45-55% 且 p>0.10（所有 judge × benchmark 组合）\n21\t- 状态：formality 69.1% (p=0.006) on GPT-4o × LLMBar ✅\n22\t\n23\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献，强化): Likert pointwise scoring 系统性低估 style bias — \"Likert Blindspot\"\n24\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：需要 sign-test on binarized Likert 控制实验来隔离 pairwise 的结构性优势 vs 统计检验选择差异。这是 C2 的命门。\n25\t- 证伪条件：binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 不在测量方法而在统计检验\n26\t- 状态：Likert p=0.332 vs Pairwise p=0.006，同一数据 ✅；binarized Likert control 待做\n27\t\n28\t### C3 (Empirical — 降级为 preliminary): Style bias 检测的可行性因 axis 语义性质而异\n29\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：只有 formality robust，\"multi-axis decomposition\" 和 \"prestige dimension\" 过度承诺。改为 \"preliminary evidence\" + \"method boundary\"。\n30\t- 新表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention 适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 style axes（formality ✅, verbosity 需适配 ✅）；改变认知承诺的 axes（tone ❌）结构性不兼容\"\n31\t- 证伪条件：所有 surface-level axes 都一样 → 无 axis 依赖性\n32\t\n33\t### C4 (Practical — 新增): CSD-based 实用建议 / 轻量 correction\n34\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：\"detection-only, no correction\" 是三档一致的弱点。需要至少提供 practitioner guidance 或 lightweight correction component。\n35\t- 方案：(a) CSD-adjusted win rate = raw_win_rate - original_preference_estimate + 50%（需正式统计模型支撑）；(b) 实用建议清单：\"use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; verify content preservation per axis; control for original preference\"\n36\t- 这不需要是完整的 debiasing 系统，但需要比纯 detection 多一步\n37\t\n38\t## Story Spine\n39\t\n40\t### Problem\n41\tLLM-as-judge 已成为 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999, Soumik bias 0.76-0.92），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n42\t\n43\t### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n44\t- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，简单有效但只处理一个维度，且提供 detection + correction\n45\t- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n46\t- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，但因果纠缠\n47\t- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — CSD 的 Stage 4 直接采用此方法（必须引用）\n48\t- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: 最近的方法论 predecessor — persona counterfactual + BT aggregation\n49\t- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap\n50\t\n51\t### Our Framing (修正)\n52\t我们用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison 检测 LLM judge 的 per-axis causal style bias。核心发现不是\"我们提出了一个新框架\"，而是**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖了 style bias（p=0.33 vs p=0.006）**，这对依赖 Likert scoring 的整个 LLM 评估生态有直接影响。\n53\t\n54\t### Headline Result Template\n55\t\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias (p={likert_p}), but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant {axis} preference ({win_rate}%, p<{p_value}) — this Likert Blindspot persists across {N} judges and {M} benchmarks.\"\n56\t\n57\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigation (Dream 更新)\n58\t\n59\t### RC1 (致命级): \"只有一个 judge 和一个 benchmark\" → exp-001, exp-002\n60\t### RC2 (重伤级): \"Likert-Pairwise gap 是统计检验选择差异不是测量方法差异\" → **exp-010 (NEW): sign-test on binarized Likert**\n61\t### RC3 (重伤级): \"方向不对称 = original preference\" → exp-005 (扩展到所有 judge×benchmark)\n62\t### RC4 (中等级): \"Novelty incremental, 组件都是已知的\" → 重新定位为 application + empirical contribution，诚实 acknowledge 组件来源\n63\t### RC5 (中等级): \"Detection-only, no correction\" → C4 (practical guidance + lightweight correction)\n64\t### RC6 (中等级): \"C3 oversold\" → 降级为 preliminary，reframe title\n65\t### RC7 (低级): \"n=100 太小\" → exp-006 (n=500) + power analysis\n66\t### RC8 (低级): \"NLI threshold arbitrary\" → exp-011 sensitivity analysis\n67\t### RC9 (低级): \"No counterfactual examples\" → 论文添加 2-3 annotated examples\n68\t\n69\t## Narrative Strategy (保持，但标题修正)\n70\t\n71\t### Type: 突破局限型 + \"普遍实践+隐藏风险\" hook\n72\t### Title: \"The Likert Blindspot\" (命名最强发现)\n73\t### Intro P2 修正: \"但我们发现标准 Likert scoring 系统性掩盖 style bias — 同一数据上 Likert 报告无偏差（p=0.33），pairwise comparison 却检测到显著偏好（p<0.01）\"\n74\t\n75\t### Figure 1: Problem illustration (Likert vs Pairwise gap) — 保持\n76\t### Figure 2: Method overview — 保持\n77\t### Main Result Table: axes (rows) × judges (cols) × {Pairwise, Likert, Binarized-Likert} — 新增 binarized Likert 列\n78\t\n79\t## Bibliography 目标\n80\t从 10 refs → 25+ refs。必须引用：RATE, Counterfactual Rhetorical, FairJudge, Veitch et al. 2020, Soumik 2026, style transfer evaluation lit (Mir et al., Krishna et al.), Chatbot Arena/FairEval, human annotation agreement studies.\n81\t\n82\t## Venue Fit\n83\tEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Dream 显示 Findings 确定可达，Main 需要：(1) binarized Likert 控制确认 C2；(2) 2+ judges significant after correction；(3) practical guidance component；(4) 25+ references。\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"220bc2fd-55ea-47bb-9e3b-27f8f504f222","uuid":"5db33a25-8094-488f-a8bf-670f3038ab86","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:13:33.243Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Dream 1 (dream_20260520T211832) 三档均 3.0/6 (Findings)。以下为 D015 修正版。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title (Dream 修正)\n**旧**: \"Causal Style Decomposition Reveals Systematic Style Bias in LLM-as-Judge That Likert Scoring Misses\"\n**新**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n- 理由：三档审稿人一致认为 \"decomposition\" 和 \"framework\" 过度承诺。新标题聚焦最强发现 (C2) 且更准确。\n\n## Core Claims (3 条 + 1 practical，修正后)\n\n### C1 (Method — 降级表述): Counterfactual pairwise comparison 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 style bias\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：不是新 \"framework\"，是已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用。论文中必须明确 acknowledge 组件来源（RATE, style transfer evaluation, MT-Bench pairwise）并定位为 application contribution。\n- 证伪条件：pairwise win rate 在 45-55% 且 p>0.10（所有 judge × benchmark 组合）\n- 状态：formality 69.1% (p=0.006) on GPT-4o × LLMBar ✅\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献，强化): Likert pointwise scoring 系统性低估 style bias — \"Likert Blindspot\"\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：需要 sign-test on binarized Likert 控制实验来隔离 pairwise 的结构性优势 vs 统计检验选择差异。这是 C2 的命门。\n- 证伪条件：binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 不在测量方法而在统计检验\n- 状态：Likert p=0.332 vs Pairwise p=0.006，同一数据 ✅；binarized Likert control 待做\n\n### C3 (Empirical — 降级为 preliminary): Style bias 检测的可行性因 axis 语义性质而异\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：只有 formality robust，\"multi-axis decomposition\" 和 \"prestige dimension\" 过度承诺。改为 \"preliminary evidence\" + \"method boundary\"。\n- 新表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention 适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 style axes（formality ✅, verbosity 需适配 ✅）；改变认知承诺的 axes（tone ❌）结构性不兼容\"\n- 证伪条件：所有 surface-level axes 都一样 → 无 axis 依赖性\n\n### C4 (Practical — 新增): CSD-based 实用建议 / 轻量 correction\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：\"detection-only, no correction\" 是三档一致的弱点。需要至少提供 practitioner guidance 或 lightweight correction component。\n- 方案：(a) CSD-adjusted win rate = raw_win_rate - original_preference_estimate + 50%（需正式统计模型支撑）；(b) 实用建议清单：\"use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; verify content preservation per axis; control for original preference\"\n- 这不需要是完整的 debiasing 系统，但需要比纯 detection 多一步\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge 已成为 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999, Soumik bias 0.76-0.92），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n\n### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，简单有效但只处理一个维度，且提供 detection + correction\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，但因果纠缠\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — CSD 的 Stage 4 直接采用此方法（必须引用）\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: 最近的方法论 predecessor — persona counterfactual + BT aggregation\n- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap\n\n### Our Framing (修正)\n我们用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison 检测 LLM judge 的 per-axis causal style bias。核心发现不是\"我们提出了一个新框架\"，而是**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖了 style bias（p=0.33 vs p=0.006）**，这对依赖 Likert scoring 的整个 LLM 评估生态有直接影响。\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias (p={likert_p}), but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant {axis} preference ({win_rate}%, p<{p_value}) — this Likert Blindspot persists across {N} judges and {M} benchmarks.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigation (Dream 更新)\n\n### RC1 (致命级): \"只有一个 judge 和一个 benchmark\" → exp-001, exp-002\n### RC2 (重伤级): \"Likert-Pairwise gap 是统计检验选择差异不是测量方法差异\" → **exp-010 (NEW): sign-test on binarized Likert**\n### RC3 (重伤级): \"方向不对称 = original preference\" → exp-005 (扩展到所有 judge×benchmark)\n### RC4 (中等级): \"Novelty incremental, 组件都是已知的\" → 重新定位为 application + empirical contribution，诚实 acknowledge 组件来源\n### RC5 (中等级): \"Detection-only, no correction\" → C4 (practical guidance + lightweight correction)\n### RC6 (中等级): \"C3 oversold\" → 降级为 preliminary，reframe title\n### RC7 (低级): \"n=100 太小\" → exp-006 (n=500) + power analysis\n### RC8 (低级): \"NLI threshold arbitrary\" → exp-011 sensitivity analysis\n### RC9 (低级): \"No counterfactual examples\" → 论文添加 2-3 annotated examples\n\n## Narrative Strategy (保持，但标题修正)\n\n### Type: 突破局限型 + \"普遍实践+隐藏风险\" hook\n### Title: \"The Likert Blindspot\" (命名最强发现)\n### Intro P2 修正: \"但我们发现标准 Likert scoring 系统性掩盖 style bias — 同一数据上 Likert 报告无偏差（p=0.33），pairwise comparison 却检测到显著偏好（p<0.01）\"\n\n### Figure 1: Problem illustration (Likert vs Pairwise gap) — 保持\n### Figure 2: Method overview — 保持\n### Main Result Table: axes (rows) × judges (cols) × {Pairwise, Likert, Binarized-Likert} — 新增 binarized Likert 列\n\n## Bibliography 目标\n从 10 refs → 25+ refs。必须引用：RATE, Counterfactual Rhetorical, FairJudge, Veitch et al. 2020, Soumik 2026, style transfer evaluation lit (Mir et al., Krishna et al.), Chatbot Arena/FairEval, human annotation agreement studies.\n\n## Venue Fit\nEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Dream 显示 Findings 确定可达，Main 需要：(1) binarized Likert 控制确认 C2；(2) 2+ judges significant after correction；(3) practical guidance component；(4) 25+ references。\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RKJRsJ3h9m69Hmu8JYufa2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the data and framing. Let me also read the paper-writing-norms skill and the distilled research/writing skills since they're relevant for writing a paper.\n\nActually, the task says this is a \"worst\" tier paper. The narrative guidance says:\n- C2 (\"Likert Blindspot\") is falsified or effect doesn't generalize\n- Binarized Likert sign test is significant (p<0.04), proving the Likert-Pairwise gap comes from statistical test power differences, not structural measurement advantages\n- Effect is limited to GPT-4o × LLMBar only; Claude/Gemini not significant; additional benchmarks don't replicate\n\n\n- I need a fundamental reframe around either sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs or the original-text preference confound as a cautionary negative result\n- C4 becomes more important here — showing what not to do is itself a contribution\n- I'm targeting EMNLP Findings (projected 2.8-3.3)\n\nSince the original hypothesis largely failed, I'm going with the original-text preference confound as the main narrative since the logistic regression data strongly supports it. I'm structuring the paper around this reframing, with a title that reflects the negative or cautionary nature of the result.\n\nThe abstract frames this as a methodological cautionary tale about confounds in style bias detection. The introduction sets up the problem of style bias in LLM judges and how the community has been studying it, then reveals that what looks like style bias is actually original-text preference. The methods section covers the counterfactual generation pipeline with NLI verification, pairwise comparison, and RATE control. Then I'm laying out the experiments across three sections: initial detection showing formality bias that doesn't generalize across judges or benchmarks, the Likert-pairwise gap as statistical rather than structural, and finally the original-text preference confound as the key finding.\n\nNow I'm writing the full LaTeX paper, making sure to ground everything in actual numbers from the experiment data and cover all twelve experiments while following the narrative reframe. I need to be rigorous about this. I'm continuing to map out the remaining experiments into their sections—the Likert-pairwise gap analysis, original-text preference confounds, scaled replication work, axis applicability boundaries, and robustness checks. Now I need to write the full paper and weave all twelve experiments into a coherent narrative that builds the argument about measurement artifacts in LLM evaluation. I'm mapping out where each experiment belongs in the paper structure, with most going into the main sections and a few ablations relegated to the appendix. Now I'll start drafting the paper with a target of eight pages for the main content.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17562,"cache_read_input_tokens":23817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17562},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"220bc2fd-55ea-47bb-9e3b-27f8f504f222","uuid":"73429f44-8f88-49b3-baca-0fbc0583086c"}
